FerrionOS change to the upstream installer (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 16d39fe1f20f15fc97fa3aaa216ac7e449637d41 after ferrion-live-disk.patch:
- the text and graphical installers encrypt the disk unless the user says no; general.install_unencrypted = true skips the question for unattended test installations.
- creating an encrypted filesystem refuses unless /scheme/rand/status reports seeded: yes.
- after the target volume is closed, redoxfs-key adds a recovery key in its own slot, which the installer shows once and asks the user to confirm they saved.
- the passphrase is no longer trimmed, and the installed filesystem.toml never holds general.encrypt_disk: it is written from the parsed configuration without it, and fast cloning falls back to copying files when the live image's configuration holds one. --output-config still writes the whole configuration.

